  "narrative": {
    "essence": "Czechia returns to the World Cup for the first time since 2006, rebuilt around a generation that grew up watching the Czech Republic punch above its weight in Europe. This squad is technically capable and tactically disciplined — not a glamour team, but one that can make life very difficult.",
    "footballIdentity": "Czech football has an understated European soul — technically sound, tactically astute, and never overwhelmed by the moment. The golden generation of Nedvěd, Poborský, and Schmeichel in the 1990s and early 2000s set a high bar. The country doesn't produce superstars the way France or Germany does, but it consistently produces reliable, intelligent professionals who understand their role.",
    "theMoment": "Czechia qualified having undergone a significant rebuild after missing the 2022 World Cup entirely. The Czech football federation, amid debates about investment in youth development and concerns about the domestic league quality, finally sees this squad as the product of better academy structures. Making the knockout rounds would vindicate a quiet revolution in Czech football infrastructure.",
    "momentType": "footballing"
  },
