    "tacticalNote": "Czechia presses from a 4-2-3-1 structure, using Souček's industry and physicality to dominate central areas. They're dangerous from set pieces — Souček and Schick are both aerial threats. Build-up is direct, using Schick's hold-up play to establish footholds, then overloading wide areas with Coufal's runs.",
    "strength": "Set piece danger and midfield physicality — Souček's influence from dead balls consistently produces goals the Czech Republic shouldn't be getting.",
    "vulnerability": "Susceptible in transitions when the double-pivot is caught high — quick teams can expose the space behind the midfield block."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Souček arriving late into the penalty area from deep — he scores 8-10 goals a season for West Ham doing exactly this.",
